    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 0.62,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.12,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 0.60-0.65 from 5 h to 18 h. A saturating reader could produce a plateau like that even while biomass kept rising. To test this, I read the 18 h aliquot at 5x dilution. It gave 0.1266, which is 0.633 after correcting for dilution. The undiluted reading was 0.605. The two differ by about 5%, which is within the plate reader's replicate scatter of about 0.01-0.02 OD, which is roughly what the undiluted hourly readings vary by. If the reader were saturating, the diluted reading scaled back up would be clearly higher than the undiluted one, and it was not. The reader therefore appears linear in this range, and the culture is in stationary phase at about OD 0.6. The budget allowed only one replicate, so this rests on a single dilution read."
  },
